Kuran Yolu — Source, License and Provenance Notice

This repository combines openly licensed source material, public-domain or
historical works, project-authored material, and AI-assisted project output.
Technical provenance is recorded in:

  docs/provenance/source-content-provenance.json

Primary source notices:

- Qur'an Arabic text: Tanzil Quran Text, Uthmani 1.1, CC BY 3.0.
  Copyright (C) 2007-2026 Tanzil Project. The canonical source is retained
  verbatim and attributed at https://tanzil.net/.
- Morphology references: Quranic Arabic Corpus v0.4 and the
  mustafa0x/quran-morphology fork; CAMeL Tools (MIT) and CAMeL Morph
  (CC BY 4.0). Kuran Yolu adds canonical token alignment, Unicode
  normalization, contextual selection, corrections and manual verification.
- Tajweed rule source: AlQuran.cloud quran-tajweed markers. Kuran Yolu
  realigns them to canonical Tanzil text and produces its own span,
  coordinate, color, validation and manual-override layer.
- Elmalılı Hamdi Yazır, Hak Dini Kur'an Dili; the digital source chain
  includes Semar Ketir's MIT-licensed JSON Quran work.
- Fonts: Amiri, Figtree and Lora under SIL OFL 1.1; UthmanicHafs under
  the embedded KFGQPC end-user license.

Kuran Yolu project contributions include Turkish word meanings, morphology
curation, tajweed alignment and overrides, presentation code, project-authored
guides, and AI-assisted translations, explanations, lessons and media. AI
tool provenance and known evidence gaps are listed in the central manifest.

The raw `morfoloji` table was removed from the runtime on 2026-07-28 and is
retained only as a hashed provenance artifact. The raw `verses.arabic_tajweed`
field is retained as the build input for tajweed span regeneration and for API
backward compatibility; rendering uses canonical text plus tajweed spans.
Elmalılı is the
only production meal; the four other meals (bulac, diyanet, ozturk, vakfi)
were removed from the runtime by a guarded migration and are retained in the
provenance manifest as removed_from_runtime.

